# Dragon Sniper (1/1, reach, vigilance, deathtouch), cast on turn 1. Turn 3: it attacks and, having vigilance, is NOT tapped
# by attacking (1 damage, Bot2 19). Turn 4: Bot2's Ornithopter (a 0/2 flier) attacks. Reach lets the Sniper block
# it; the Llanowar Elves, which has no reach, cannot (refusal, with the Sniper's own block as the positive control). The
# Sniper's single point of deathtouch damage destroys the 0/2 Ornithopter (a plain 1 damage would not); the Ornithopter
# deals 0, so the Sniper lives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Dragon Sniper
Llanowar Elves
Island x4
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dragon Sniper.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Dragon Sniper > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dragon Sniper.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Life = 19
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.DeclareBlockers]
! Bot1.Block(Llanowar Elves > Ornithopter)
Bot1.Block(Dragon Sniper > Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Dragon Sniper; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Dragon Sniper.Damage = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 19
